//! Briefing redesign B2 (wave-3 plan R5-H1): the engine↔Rust private-facts contract, Rust side.
//!
//! `action_facts_contract` reads the shared, checked-in fixture `fixtures/action-facts-vectors.json`
//! (never regenerated by a test: the engine's `test/repos.targets.test.ts` compares real facts with the
//! same literal) and parses its `actionFacts` through the PRODUCTION facts parser
//! (`repos::parse_action_facts`) into held facts. A shape the parser cannot read would otherwise degrade
//! to empty facts, and so to `actions: []` and no buttons, with every other suite green.
//!
//! T5 built the parse stage, T6 the mint and T7 the stamp acceptance. One recording-sink click per sink (T8, T9, T11)
//! extends this test. The `t6_` tests below pin the rules each handle is minted by, the `t8_` and `t9_` tests what a
//! click on one opens, copies or refuses. T11's own rules are in `tests/editor.rs`.
//!
//! No test here reads the user's repos, HOME or git config. The fixture's paths are `/fixture` placeholders; the stamp
//! tests materialise them under their own scratch directory (`common::materialise_action_facts`, plan P-H1).

